---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  path="/en/privacy"
  altPath="/privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy · Law Portal"
  description="How Law Portal collects, uses, and protects your personal data, in line with Saudi Arabia's Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL)."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-warning bg-warning-tint p-4 text-sm text-ink">
      <strong>Note:</strong> this is a first-draft template for this stage of the product, not final legal text. It
      must be reviewed by counsel specializing in Saudi Arabia's Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) before a real
      launch.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-soft">
      <p>Last updated: <span class="font-mono">2026-08-03</span></p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">1. Data we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We collect account data (name, phone number or email, a hashed password), lawyer licence data (licence
          number, issue and expiry dates), request and message content tied to the legal service requested, and
          payment data (via a licensed payment gateway — we never store full card details on our own servers).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">2. Basis and purpose of processing</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We process your data to perform our contract with you (delivering the requested legal service), to comply
          with statutory obligations (such as tax invoicing), and for our legitimate interest in improving and
          securing the platform. Legal correspondence data is never used for marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">3. Data sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Your request data is shared only with the lawyer assigned to that request. We use trusted service
          providers (payment gateway, cloud hosting, SMS provider) as data processors on our behalf, under data
          processing agreements, and we never sell your data to any third party for marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">4. Data retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We retain account and request data for as long as the account is active, and financial/invoicing records
          for the period required under Saudi tax and accounting regulation, even after account deletion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">5. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can request access to or correction of your data from your account settings. You may also request
          full account deletion; your personal data is deleted immediately, except for records the law requires us
          to retain, such as tax invoices.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">6. Data transfer outside the Kingdom</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Some supporting technical systems (such as voice/video calling) are hosted on infrastructure with local
          data residency wherever possible, specifically because of the sensitivity of legal content. Any transfer
          of data outside the Kingdom is carried out under the terms permitted by the Personal Data Protection Law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">7. Contact us</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">For any privacy-related question, please reach us at the email listed in the page footer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
